error[E0913]: a macro can't add fields to `Hero`
  --> tests/ui/macro_item_errors.wid:72:14
   |
72 |   add_field :mana
   |              ^^^^ `add_field` generates this field
   = note: a struct's layout is fixed before the macros in its body run, which is what lets them read `Self.fields`
help: declare `mana` in `Hero` itself, and let the macro generate the methods that use it
   = see `wid explain E0913`

error[E0209]: `type_name` needs one `Self`, but here it stands for many types
  --> tests/ui/macro_item_errors.wid:76:3
   |
36 |   name = Self.name
   |          ---- the macro's code uses `Self` here
...
76 |   type_name
   |   ^^^^^^^^^ `type_name` expands here, where `Self` has no single type
   = note: in a `module` or `extend` body, `Self` is each type that includes or is extended by it, and in a generic struct's body it is each instance; a macro runs once for the call, so it can't use all of them
help: call `type_name` in the body or a method of a `struct` or `enum`, or give the macro a `Type` parameter and pass the type
   = see `wid explain E0209`

error[E0209]: `named` needs one `Self`, but here it stands for many types
  --> tests/ui/macro_item_errors.wid:77:3
   |
77 |   named Self
   |   ^^^^^^^^^^ `named` expands here, where `Self` has no single type
   |         ---- this argument is `Self`
   = note: in a `module` or `extend` body, `Self` is each type that includes or is extended by it, and in a generic struct's body it is each instance; a macro runs once for the call, so it can't use all of them
help: pass a named type instead of `Self`, or call `named` in the body of each type that needs it
   = see `wid explain E0209`

