error[E0209]: `type_name` needs a `Self`, but this call has none
  --> tests/ui/macro_item_errors.wid:91:1
   |
36 |   name = Self.name
   |          ---- the macro's code uses `Self` here
...
91 | type_name
   | ^^^^^^^^^ `type_name` expands here, outside any type
   = note: a macro's `Self` is the type whose body or method holds the call
help: call `type_name` in the body or a method of a `struct` or `enum`, or give the macro a `Type` parameter and pass the type
   = see `wid explain E0209`

error[E0108]: statements must be inside a method
  --> tests/ui/macro_item_errors.wid:93:1
   |
93 | helper
   | ^^^^^^ this call is outside any `def`
   = note: `helper` is a method, not a macro; only a macro call can stand among declarations
help: move it into `def main … end`, which runs when the program starts
   = see `wid explain E0108`

error[E0201]: undefined macro `undefined_macro`
  --> tests/ui/macro_item_errors.wid:94:1
   |
94 | undefined_macro :x
   | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ no macro with this name is in scope
   = note: a call among declarations runs a macro, and the declarations it generates take the call's place
   = see `wid explain E0201`

error[E0328]: `@[inline]` doesn't apply to a macro call
  --> tests/ui/macro_item_errors.wid:95:3
   |
95 | @[inline] nothing
   |   ^^^^^^ a macro call takes no attributes
   = note: attributes belong on the declarations the macro generates
help: remove `@[inline]`, or write it on the declarations inside the macro's `quote`
   = see `wid explain E0328`

error[E0108]: statements must be inside a method
  --> tests/ui/macro_item_errors.wid:96:1
   |
96 | puts "hi"
   | ^^^^^^^^^ this call is outside any `def`
help: move it into `def main … end`, which runs when the program starts
   = see `wid explain E0108`

error[E0201]: undefined macro `blue`
  --> tests/ui/macro_item_errors.wid:63:5
   |
63 |     blue
   |     ^^^^ no macro with this name is in scope
  ::: tests/ui/macro_item_errors.wid:87:3
   |
87 |   member()
   |   -------- `member` expands here
   = note: a call among declarations runs a macro, and the declarations it generates take the call's place
   = note: an enum's members are fixed before the macros in its body run, so a macro can't add members
help: list the member in the enum itself, or have a macro called at package level generate the whole `enum`
   = see `wid explain E0201`

error[E0108]: statements must be inside a method
  --> tests/ui/macro_item_errors.wid:29:5
   |
29 |     count = 1
   |     ^^^^^^^^^ this statement is outside any `def`
  ::: tests/ui/macro_item_errors.wid:90:1
   |
90 | statements
   | ---------- `statements` expands here
   = note: `statements` is called among declarations, so its code must be declarations: methods, constants, types, `include`s or macro calls
help: put the statement inside a `def` in the `quote`, or call `statements` inside a method
   = see `wid explain E0108`

